      <h2 id="limits">What collagen peptides do not do</h2>

      <p>
        They do not treat disease, they do not regrow cartilage, and they do not work fast. This
        section exists because the gap between what the trials showed and what the category claims
        is wide enough to be worth stating plainly, even on a page that sells a collagen product.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>No cartilage regrowth.</strong> No trial has demonstrated that oral collagen peptides regrow cartilage in humans. What they have shown is reduced pain and better function. Any brand claiming regrowth is describing a result nobody has produced.</li>
        <li><strong>Not a treatment for arthritis.</strong> Collagen peptides support tissue that is under load. They do not modify the course of osteoarthritis or of any inflammatory arthritis, and rheumatoid arthritis in particular needs disease-modifying drugs, not a shot.</li>
        <li><strong>Not a complete protein.</strong> Collagen contains no tryptophan and is low in several other essential amino acids. It cannot be counted towards your protein requirement in the way dal, paneer, eggs or whey can.</li>
        <li><strong>Not proven to reverse ageing.</strong> Measured elasticity and hydration improved in trials lasting weeks. That is not the same as reversing anything, and the effect faded after supplementation stopped.</li>
        <li><strong>Not for everyone.</strong> Marine peptides come from fish, so anyone with a fish or shellfish allergy should avoid them. If you are pregnant, breastfeeding, on prescription medication or have chronic kidney disease, ask your own doctor before adding a gram-level protein supplement.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        One product-specific disclosure while I am at it. Skelecoll contains 300mg of glucosamine
        HCl, and the glucosamine monotherapy trials used 1,500mg. That 300mg is a supporting
        co-factor inside a stack built around the 10g collagen dose, and it should not be read as a
        glucosamine therapy. If you want to test high-dose glucosamine on its own merits, buy it
        separately at 1,500mg and judge it over three months.
      </p>

